sistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.09028163546679338,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":46.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.21896569469878008,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.1821134086684093,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-3.28925936452001,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.04137272415345916,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.057348362187071865,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":4.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.04502,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":30.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.182,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":18.2,"pf":[],"description_full":"Gevo, Inc. operates as a carbon abatement company. It operates in four segments: Gevo, GevoFuels, GevoRNG, and GevoND. The company offers sustainable aviation fuel, motor fuels, and chemicals and materials; certain specialty fuels, on-road fuels, and certain products for the food chain comprising protein and feeds; hydrocarbons for gasoline, racing fuel blend stocks, and diesel fuel; ethylene and butenes; plastics and materials; and renewable natural gas, isobutanol, and isooctane. It is also involved in development, construction, and operation of Alcohol-to-Jet projects; provision of GevoRNG, a project which leverages anaerobic digestion technology to capture and convert methane emissions into renewable natural gas; and operates Verity platform that tracks, measures, and verifies various attributes throughout the supply chain. In addition, it offers products manufactured by ethanol plant, including ethanol and distillers grains. The company was formerly known as Methanotech, Inc. and changed its name to Gevo, Inc. in March 2006. Gevo, Inc. was incorporated in 2005 and is headquartered in Englewood, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Paul D. Bloom | CEO, President & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 151 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $61K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Gevo, Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $453M market cap on $161M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +415% over the past three years and +18% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -22% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and -36% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $44M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 16.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 583% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":5.832107990840062},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (82% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.182},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Basic Materials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Stocks making big moves this week: Gevo, AAON, Lincoln Educational, Azenta, and Coinbase","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/gevo/news/why-it-moves-summary/stocks-making-big-moves-this-week-gevo-aaon-lincoln-educational-azenta-and-coinbase","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794574844.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Does Gevo (NASDAQ:GEVO) Gain From Its Record Carbon Quarter?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/s